      "writtenOn": "2019-08-13T22:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Judging by how the STM32 code does it [1], I think the I2C files should only be added if `CONFIG_I2C` is defined, something like this:\n\n chip-$(CONFIG_I2C)+\u003di2c_chip.o i2c_api.o\n\nOtherwise, I get compile errors saying that `CC_I2C` is undefined when I compile a board that uses the MAX32660 but doesn\u0027t define `CONFIG_I2C`.\n\n[1]: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/chip/ish/build.mk#21",
